ion: This task helps to ensure that Python and sudo are installed on the system before proceeding.\n\n### 4. Gather ansible facts\n- Description: Gathers facts about the system using the `setup` module.\n- Execution: This helps in understanding the current state of the system before proceeding with further tasks.\n\n### 5. Install bootstrap packages (package)\n- Description: Installs a list of packages specified in the `bootstrap_facts_packages` variable.\n- Execution: This task uses the `package` module and updates the cache to ensure that the latest package information is used.\n\n## Usage\n\nTo use this playbook in an Ansible Role under the `tasks/` directory, copy and paste the contents of the provided YAML file into your `tasks/main.yml` file. The playbook should start with \'---\' and a line break.' additional_kwargs={} response_metadata={'model': 'codestral:22b', 'created_at': '2025-10-18T23:16:38.520145919Z', 'done': True, 'done_reason': 'stop', 'total_duration': 14792535316, 'load_duration': 21535597, 'prompt_eval_count': 551, 'prompt_eval_duration': 465413390, 'eval_count': 724, 'eval_duration': 14304710453, 'model_name': 'codestral:22b'} id='run--e2037845-06f1-4dde-b75b-c82a5378c073-0' usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 551, 'output_tokens': 724, 'total_tokens': 1275}
